<mxCell id="s1324" value="Negating count flips only that field (high counts first); ties fall through to name, A to Z. fig and kiwi tie on −5, so &#x27;fig&#x27; &lt; &#x27;kiwi&#x27; decides." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="246" width="820" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="s1325" value="&lt;b&gt;Can&#x27;t negate a field?&lt;/b&gt; (a string you want Z to A) Sort twice relying on stability (secondary key first), or use &lt;b&gt;functools.cmp_to_key&lt;/b&gt; with a three-way compare: by length, then reverse alphabetical → [&#x27;c&#x27;, &#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;cc&#x27;, &#x27;bb&#x27;]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="290" width="820" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
