<mxCell id="s1962" value="heap size ≤ K, so each item costs O(log K): &lt;b&gt;O(N log K)&lt;/b&gt; total, O(K) memory, and it streams.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;External sort: sort RAM-sized chunks, write each as a sorted run, then K-way merge the runs." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="330" width="180" height="192" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="s1963" value="Python: heapq.merge(*lists) is the lazy K-way merge; sorted(a + b) also works well because Timsort finds the existing runs." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=13;align=left;spacingLeft=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="534" width="820" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
